<span id="Linus_Pauling_(1901.E2.80.931994)"></span><div mt-section-origin="Courses/Howard_University/General_Chemistry:_An_Atoms_First_Approach/Unit_1:__Atomic_Structure/Chapter_3:__The_Periodic_Table/Chapter_3.3:_Energetics_of_Ion_Formation" class="mt-section"><span id="Linus_Pauling_(1901.E2.80.931994)"></span><h3 id="Linus_Pauling_(1901.E2.80.931994)-17436">Linus Pauling (1901&ndash;1994)</h3>

<p class="para" id="av_1.0-ch03_s03_s03_s01_p04">Pauling won two Nobel Prizes, one for chemistry in 1954 and one for peace in 1962. When he was nine, Pauling&rsquo;s father died, and his mother tried to convince him to quit school to support the family. He did not quit school but was denied a high school degree because of his refusal to take a civics class.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="figure large" id="av_1.0-ch03_s03_s03_s01_f02">
